# The patch inventory: every file outside the fork's own directories that
# differs from the postgres/postgres commit the fork last merged.
#
# Merging a new upstream release means re-examining each of these files, so
# each one is listed here with the reason the fork changes it.  The check
# in check_patch_inventory.sh fails when a changed file is missing from this
# list, when a listed file no longer differs from upstream, or when a line
# is malformed.
#
# Two kinds of line:
#
#   own   PATH
#       PATH belongs to the fork alone; nothing under it (if it ends in /)
#       or nothing at it (if it doesn't) is a core change.
#
#   patch PATH LAYER REASON...
#       PATH is a core file the fork changes.  LAYER is the roadmap layer
#       that needs the change; REASON is a one-line explanation.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.  Keep each section
# sorted by path.

# The fork's own files.
own   .github/README.md
own   .github/workflows/prolly-upstream-sync.yml
own   .github/workflows/prolly.yml
